Subject: [PATCH 6/7] FlyWeb 3.2.0 interface: Shields as a colored shield
 outline with the count

From Titin's design (softmac FlyWeb/branding/interfaz-3.2.0): the Shields
button draws the outline of ico-escudo.svg (no fly) as a vector instead
of the IDR_FLYWEB_SHIELDS_ICON_* PNGs:
- green with Shields up on the site, red with Shields down,
- the neutral icon color on pages where Shields does not act (internal
  and local schemes), which used to share the "down" image,
- the blocked count inside the shield up to 99; above it, "99+" in the
  usual badge outside.
The button sits inside the URL field, so the colors are chosen for the
field background (one pair for a light field, one for a dark field).
Values are provisional constants (kFlyWebShields*) until Titin sees
them. The icon is also refreshed on theme changes, since the colors come
from the color provider.

